findings.claim:
The extraction has no item for five notions that every main statement or its proof uses:
- **quasi-excellent schemes:** hypotheses of Theorems 1.2.5, 1.2.9, 4.2.1 and 4.3.1;
- **universally Japanese schemes:** Lemma 3.3.4, Theorem 3.3.6;
- **regular schemes:** every conclusion;
- **snc divisors:** every conclusion, and 'snc divisor' as the support of one (Exposé X convention);
- **the quotient Y/G of a scheme by a finite group:** the definition of Galois alterations in §3.3.1, and (X̄, T̄)/G in Step 10 of Theorem 4.2.1.
Neither library has any of these. In the atlas:
- quasi-excellence appears in no stage;
- regular schemes are owned by Tau Ceti ModularCurves 4D;
- the Japanese property is planned only for k[X] (AlgebraicCurves Layer 2);
- finite quotients only for affine schemes and free actions (ModularCurves 0C).
The non-free quotient glued from invariant affines, which Step 10 needs (SGA 1, V.1), has no owner.
